    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on exploiting high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, specifically targeting the 5.16 xERA of the Houston starter. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) stands out as our premier start; the combination of a high-value lineup spot and a significant SP skill boost creates an elite environment for him today. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) are anchors for our offensive production, with both benefiting from park factors and favorable platoon splits that push their efficiency scores well into the \"Strong\" tier. **JJ Bleday** is a particularly interesting play at 66.17; despite batting seventh, his matchup against a 6.01 xERA arm allows him to overcome the order penalty, making him an ideal source of volume scoring for today\u2019s 5x5 objectives.\n\nOur toughest bench decision centered on **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.89), who hovered near the threshold but ultimately fell short due to a negative platoon adjustment against the opposing lefty. While **Jung Hoo Lee** offers the type of high-contact profile we value, his projected efficiency simply didn't clear the bar set by **Gavin Sheets** and **Justin Crawford** in their respective matchups. We remain wary of **Cal Raleigh** (56.88), whose score is tethered to a tough battle against a 3.69 xERA arm in Imanaga; while he is in the lineup for his power potential, his performance is the most susceptible to a low-scoring game script. With **Daulton Varsho** and **Braden Montgomery** both cooling their heels on the bench, we are prioritizing the high-xERA exposure of the active starters to maximize our run and RBI potential while keeping an eye on the scarcity of stolen bases that **Justin Crawford** is tasked with helping us address.",
